{"2096780": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "CRT7", "steam_appid": 2096780, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An impossible object lost to time. An eerie basement hiding an untold story. A seemingly innocent game begging to be played. That's what greets you when the elevator doors open and you stare into a room you've been trying to find for years. Just what <i>happened</i> down here? Only you can find out by exploring this abandoned room and unlocking the devices strewn around it. Point, click, flick, and rotate your way through a huge variety of different types of puzzles safe in the knowledge there is an in-built hint system if you ever get stuck. That old monitor glowing in the distance looks like a good place to start... </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/928254197b28e424ccaf89bddbfbc4eb.poster.avif?t=1779919415\" aria-label=\"A video showing an old CRT monitor sitting on a desk, with a strange device next to it covered in glowing green 7-segment displays, and two dials or timers in the middle. The screen shows an amber-coloured interface that has CRT7 rendered in ascii symbols. A mouse cursor moves to what seems to be a play button, before a new menu is selected. The cursor then moves over a jigsaw-piece button and the following text appears: &quot;POTENTIAL. Think carefully. Think carefully. No time limit. Regret limitations. INVERT the past&quot;. The cursor then moves over an hour glass icon and the following text appears: &quot;KINETIC. Race the clock. Stamp pentominoes. Create 3x3 quads. Regret the past. COMBOS are valuable.&quot; The cursor then clicks a back button to go to the original screen and the video loops.\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/928254197b28e424ccaf89bddbfbc4eb.webm?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/928254197b28e424ccaf89bddbfbc4eb.mp4?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome to CRT7, an escape room puzzle game about power, obsession, and regret from the award-winning creator of SOLAS 128.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The core loop is simple:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Figure out how the monitor works</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Play games to generate power and bring the room back to life</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore the room and decypher mysterious devices to progress</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Uncover why you are here...</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/581583f782ec4e3cf4eff92d4078fdad.poster.avif?t=1779919415\" aria-label=\"A video showing a desk with a cherry wood or red leather top. On the left is a light fixture with a large spherical bulb at the top, with a base with gold inlays. On top of it sits a golden pentomino. The main focus is on some sort of &#039;Hi-7&#039; tape player. On the front are several pairs of up and down arrows with grey cross between them. Each time a button is clicked a different coloured symbol appears instead of the cross, from all the primary and secondary colours of light. At the end, a cursor clicks a play button and it resets.\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/581583f782ec4e3cf4eff92d4078fdad.webm?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/581583f782ec4e3cf4eff92d4078fdad.mp4?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Procedurally generated music which reacts to you playing </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A dark narrative about creation to piece together </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At least one (1) fully rendered 3D room to explore </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Strange retro devices to prod and poke </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A state-of-the-art* in-game phone with a hint systems and photographic note-taking </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A huge variety of puzzles to create a challenging mystery for fans of escape rooms </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An immersive and creepy atmosphere with no jump scares </p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >*for 2010 </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/95126435d1036038d9f264f455b3f358.poster.avif?t=1779919415\" aria-label=\"A video showing a view into a room harshly lit with orange light. On the wall is a strange art deco device. It is square and has a wood frame, but in the middle there is a square gold element that defines a grid of little screens. On the screens a red diamond, a green checkerboard, and a pair of blue chevrons move across the screens in discrete steps. The start at the bottom, &#039;reflect&#039; off of mirrors in the grid, then move left or right afterwards. The video seamlessly loops so the symbols move forever.\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/95126435d1036038d9f264f455b3f358.webm?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/95126435d1036038d9f264f455b3f358.mp4?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Accessibility Features:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >CRT7 has been made with consideration of accessibility from the ground up. Below are the major features, but please try the demo to make sure the game is playable for you!</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > No reliance on colour alone for any puzzle </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > No musical ability or tone recognition required for any puzzle </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > All speech is subtitled by default </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > A full hint system including text hints, hotspot identification, and in game note-taking</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Rebind the mouse clicks to keys, or controller buttons </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Change movement modes to help with motion sickness </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Override monitor colours and/or add extra light to help avoid eye strain </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Change in-game hand-written text to printed format for easier reading </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Change the size of the cursors to make them more or less visible </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > An option to reduce light flickering  effects </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Some games have timers, but you can play games multiple times to progress </p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Creators:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Amicable Animal</i> – Developer &amp; Designer</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Luci Holland</i> – Additional music &amp; sound</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/554eaf3301d4463a187cd568a3c90f7d.poster.avif?t=1779919415\" aria-label=\"A video showing a wooden door set into a wall with a dado rail. The wall has off white fabric wall paper on the top half and avocado green on the bottom half. On the door there are two eyes, stacked vertically looking around frantically. Subtitles below show &quot;back to the beginning&quot; and &quot;start again&quot; as an arrow draws itself pointing to a light switch. At the end the eyes blink and that restarts the video loop.\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/554eaf3301d4463a187cd568a3c90f7d.webm?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/554eaf3301d4463a187cd568a3c90f7d.mp4?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An impossible object lost to time. An eerie basement hiding an untold story. A seemingly innocent game begging to be played. That's what greets you when the elevator doors open and you stare into a room you've been trying to find for years. Just what <i>happened</i> down here? Only you can find out by exploring this abandoned room and unlocking the devices strewn around it. Point, click, flick, and rotate your way through a huge variety of different types of puzzles safe in the knowledge there is an in-built hint system if you ever get stuck. That old monitor glowing in the distance looks like a good place to start... </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/928254197b28e424ccaf89bddbfbc4eb.poster.avif?t=1779919415\" aria-label=\"A video showing an old CRT monitor sitting on a desk, with a strange device next to it covered in glowing green 7-segment displays, and two dials or timers in the middle. The screen shows an amber-coloured interface that has CRT7 rendered in ascii symbols. A mouse cursor moves to what seems to be a play button, before a new menu is selected. The cursor then moves over a jigsaw-piece button and the following text appears: &quot;POTENTIAL. Think carefully. Think carefully. No time limit. Regret limitations. INVERT the past&quot;. The cursor then moves over an hour glass icon and the following text appears: &quot;KINETIC. Race the clock. Stamp pentominoes. Create 3x3 quads. Regret the past. COMBOS are valuable.&quot; The cursor then clicks a back button to go to the original screen and the video loops.\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/928254197b28e424ccaf89bddbfbc4eb.webm?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/928254197b28e424ccaf89bddbfbc4eb.mp4?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Welcome to CRT7, an escape room puzzle game about power, obsession, and regret from the award-winning creator of SOLAS 128.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The core loop is simple:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Figure out how the monitor works</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Play games to generate power and bring the room back to life</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore the room and decypher mysterious devices to progress</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Uncover why you are here...</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/581583f782ec4e3cf4eff92d4078fdad.poster.avif?t=1779919415\" aria-label=\"A video showing a desk with a cherry wood or red leather top. On the left is a light fixture with a large spherical bulb at the top, with a base with gold inlays. On top of it sits a golden pentomino. The main focus is on some sort of &#039;Hi-7&#039; tape player. On the front are several pairs of up and down arrows with grey cross between them. Each time a button is clicked a different coloured symbol appears instead of the cross, from all the primary and secondary colours of light. At the end, a cursor clicks a play button and it resets.\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/581583f782ec4e3cf4eff92d4078fdad.webm?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/581583f782ec4e3cf4eff92d4078fdad.mp4?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Procedurally generated music which reacts to you playing </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A dark narrative about creation to piece together </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At least one (1) fully rendered 3D room to explore </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Strange retro devices to prod and poke </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A state-of-the-art* in-game phone with a hint systems and photographic note-taking </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A huge variety of puzzles to create a challenging mystery for fans of escape rooms </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An immersive and creepy atmosphere with no jump scares </p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >*for 2010 </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/95126435d1036038d9f264f455b3f358.poster.avif?t=1779919415\" aria-label=\"A video showing a view into a room harshly lit with orange light. On the wall is a strange art deco device. It is square and has a wood frame, but in the middle there is a square gold element that defines a grid of little screens. On the screens a red diamond, a green checkerboard, and a pair of blue chevrons move across the screens in discrete steps. The start at the bottom, &#039;reflect&#039; off of mirrors in the grid, then move left or right afterwards. The video seamlessly loops so the symbols move forever.\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/95126435d1036038d9f264f455b3f358.webm?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/95126435d1036038d9f264f455b3f358.mp4?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Accessibility Features:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >CRT7 has been made with consideration of accessibility from the ground up. Below are the major features, but please try the demo to make sure the game is playable for you!</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > No reliance on colour alone for any puzzle </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > No musical ability or tone recognition required for any puzzle </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > All speech is subtitled by default </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > A full hint system including text hints, hotspot identification, and in game note-taking</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Rebind the mouse clicks to keys, or controller buttons </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Change movement modes to help with motion sickness </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Override monitor colours and/or add extra light to help avoid eye strain </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Change in-game hand-written text to printed format for easier reading </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Change the size of the cursors to make them more or less visible </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > An option to reduce light flickering  effects </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Some games have timers, but you can play games multiple times to progress </p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Creators:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Amicable Animal</i> – Developer &amp; Designer</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Luci Holland</i> – Additional music &amp; sound</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/554eaf3301d4463a187cd568a3c90f7d.poster.avif?t=1779919415\" aria-label=\"A video showing a wooden door set into a wall with a dado rail. The wall has off white fabric wall paper on the top half and avocado green on the bottom half. On the door there are two eyes, stacked vertically looking around frantically. Subtitles below show &quot;back to the beginning&quot; and &quot;start again&quot; as an arrow draws itself pointing to a light switch. At the end the eyes blink and that restarts the video loop.\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/554eaf3301d4463a187cd568a3c90f7d.webm?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/extras/554eaf3301d4463a187cd568a3c90f7d.mp4?t=1779919415\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p>", "short_description": "Decypher strange computers, unravel modified tape players, and unlock impossible doors. Point and click your way around a mysterious basement in this challenging escape room game! Can you uncover what secrets are hiding in the dark when even time and space are against you?", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "reviews": "“I really, really enjoyed playing CRT7 and cannot wait for it’s full release. It’s part escape room, part detective game, part procedural music game and part Y2K retro goodness.”<br>The Escape Roomer<br><br>“Behind the brilliantly done atmosphere of the game you can find lots of clever puzzles, from simple games you can play on the old computer, cryptic ciphers hidden in notebooks, escape room style physical puzzles, and many more”<br>Thinky Games<br>", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/81030d138b5e3fc4f257623a228d74d44626673d/header.jpg?t=1779919415", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/8cefe2fbfd98b7b538640e89261d6e9110165120/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1779919415", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2096780/8cefe2fbfd98b7b538640e89261d6e9110165120/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1779919415", "website": "http://www.crt7game.com/", "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS *:</strong> Windows 7 or higher<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i5-4690<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> GeForce MX250<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 2 GB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong> Recommended</li></ul>", "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10 or higher<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i5-10400<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Geforce GTX 1050<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 2 GB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong> Recommended</li></ul>"}, "mac_requirements": [], "linux_requirements": [], "developers": ["Amicable Animal"], "publishers": ["Amicable Animal"], "demos": [{"appid": 2449470, "description": ""}], "package_groups": [], "platforms": {"windows": true, "mac": false, "linux": false}, "categories": [{"id": 2, "description": "Single-player"}, {"id": 22, "d